# Per-Dockerfile ignore for the `base` worker image (PRD #39 Decision 5). BuildKit
# picks this up because it is named "<Dockerfile-name>.dockerignore" and sits next
# to templates/base/Dockerfile; its patterns are resolved relative to the BUILD
# CONTEXT ROOT (the repo root, per docker-compose agent.build.context: .), NOT this
# directory. Verified: a named-Dockerfile ignore IS honored and IS context-root
# relative (a root .dockerignore would apply only as a fallback if this were absent).
#
# The agent image bakes uzi's own source read-only at /opt/uzi-src (COPY . ...), so
# unlike the web image's root .dockerignore this must NOT exclude api/ web/ agent/
# docs/ specs/ prds/ e2e/ scripts/ *.md — those ARE the source the chat agent reads.
# It only hard-excludes secrets, VCS, submodules, deps, and build artifacts.

# Secrets — must NEVER enter the build context (the baked source is world-readable
# to the agent). `.env*` (no trailing dot) also catches non-dotted forms like a
# devbox/direnv `.envrc`; `**/.env*` catches any depth including the root.
.env*
**/.env*

# VCS + submodule metadata + the large inspiration/ submodules (prior-art only).
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
inspiration/

# Installed deps + build artifacts (regenerated; not source). node_modules is huge
# and platform-specific; web/agent both list explicit paths for clarity.
**/node_modules
web/node_modules
agent/node_modules
**/dist
web/dist
agent/dist
